// Dar v3.21/v3.22 — the platform's legal texts, the same for the whole world: the Acceptable Use Policy, the Privacy Policy,
// the Terms and Conditions, the Refund Policy and (v3.22) the Partner Programme Terms. No country is named in them: the operator's own name, country and contact
// are shown at the top of each page from «Public pages → Main site → Company details», and the texts point to «the top of this page».
// Written in Arabic (the text that prevails), English and French, paragraph by paragraph: every other language reads them
// through the site's own translation (assets/core.js L/tr → dar-lang.php), translated the first time someone opens them in it.
// The owner decided (2026-10-13): a full refund within 14 days of the first payment; an annual subscription that is cancelled
// runs to the end of its year; the law of the operator's country, the consumer's mandatory rights kept; the Arabic text
// prevails; an account left read-only for 60 days is deleted (warned 30 and 7 days before); the AI providers' use of what
// they receive is said plainly; liability is capped at what was paid in the last month; changes are announced 30 days ahead.
// Every statement about how Dar works was checked against its code (masking, memory switches, the partner's view, the
// subscription's lifecycle, what deletion keeps, the measurement tags). A text the owner writes himself in «Legal texts»
// (d_legal) for one language replaces the built-in one in that language only.
// the day each text last changed (v3.22: the privacy policy and the terms name the partner programme, the use policy no longer
// reads as if partners resold the platform — they promote it for a commission; its own terms are new)
